// trap: .on_delete(cascade) keeps its one-row delete, and DanglingKey reports what it leaves.
// The lifecycle does not run a cascade yet: CancelDraft deletes the Order and no line, and
// no guard waits for the lines, since the database would remove them. The line that stays
// names an Order that is gone, so DanglingKey_OrderLine_Order fails after Open, AddLine,
// CancelDraft. The info DeleteLeavesChildren names the use case. An engine that put the
// restrict guard on a cascade key would find no counterexample. z3 meets the same step from
// a state where the rule holds, so the rule is unproved.
// expect DanglingKey_OrderLine_Order: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample z3=unproved
entity Order "注文" { id: Int @pk }
entity OrderLine "明細" { id: Int @pk }
relate(OrderLine, Order, N:1).on_delete(cascade)
usecase Open "起票"
usecase AddLine "明細追加"
usecase CancelDraft "下書き取消"
creates(Open, Order)
creates(AddLine, OrderLine)
deletes(CancelDraft, Order)
